ction appears once.\nA vertical bar chart titled \"Distribution by category\", with one bar per category (all seven always shown, including those with 0), a different colour per bar, and the count written above each bar. The Y axis must show whole numbers only (0, 1, 2, 3...), never decimals such as 0.5 or 0.25, even when there are only one or two recommendations. Set the axis to integer ticks with a minimum of 0 and a step of 1.\nRecommendations screen: a page title and short subtitle, filters for category and status, one \"Add recommendation\" button, and a table bound to Recommendation showing all five attributes, with Edit and Delete, sorting and pagination.\n\nAdd recommendation screen: a form bound to Recommendation with dropdowns for category and status and a date input for added_on, and a Save button.\n\nDesign: modern, clean and appealing. Use a soft indigo-to-sky-blue gradient on the banner, a light neutral page background, white rounded cards with a subtle shadow and a gentle hover lift, and generous, even spacing between sections. Use a harmonious palette for the categories and chart bars: indigo, sky blue, teal, amber, coral, violet, slate. Use one consistent font, and highlight the current page in the navigation bar. No authentication and no agents.\n\n## Subsequent user request, verbatim\n\nThis later request takes precedence where it changes earlier requirements.\n\nTHE CODE\n\n## Subsequent user request, verbatim\n\nThis later request takes precedence where it changes earlier requirements.\n\nthe new categories are not included in the app!!",
